  <header class="hero">
    <h1>Voter turnout low in Thurston and Dakota counties</h1>
  </header>

  <section id="body">

<p>By Mackenzie Evans</p>

<p>In Northeast Nebraska, Thurston and Dakota counties have had the lowest voter turnouts in the state from 2020 to 2026, with Thurston County frequently recording the lowest turnout.</p>

<p>Thurston County is also home to the reservations of the Winnebago and Omaha tribes of Nebraska. According to the 2020 U.S. Census, the county is 60% Native American.</p>

<p>Low voter turnout in Thurston County could mean the Native American vote is less equally represented in Nebraska.</p>

